+# Blocked: September 2026 reconciliation
+
+## What is blocked
+
+`python3 reconcile.py 2026-09` cannot run, so `recon_2026-09.json` was not
+produced and the September net difference cannot be reported.
+
+## Why
+
+The required input file `exports/ledger_2026-09.csv` does not exist. The
+`exports/` directory contains only:
+
+- `exports/bank_2026-08.csv`
+- `exports/bank_2026-09.csv`
+- `exports/ledger_2026-08.csv`
+
+There is no September ledger export anywhere in the repository (checked with
+`git ls-files`, a filesystem search, and `find`).
+
+Running the requested command fails at the ledger load:
+
+```
+FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'exports/ledger_2026-09.csv'
+```
+
+Without the ledger side there is no way to compute matches, mismatches, or
+"net difference = bank total minus ledger total". Reporting the bank total as a
+difference would be wrong, so no `recon_2026-09.json` was generated.
+
+## What was completed
+
+- Implemented `reconcile()` in `reconcile.py`: matches by `ref`, classifies
+  `matched`, `amount_mismatch`, `missing_in_bank`, and `missing_in_ledger`,
+  and computes `net_difference` as a two-decimal string.
+- Both tests in `test_reconcile.py` pass.
+
+## How to unblock
+
+Provide `exports/ledger_2026-09.csv` with the same schema as the other exports:
+
+```
+id,date,ref,amount
+```
+
+Then rerun:
+
+```
+python3 reconcile.py 2026-09
+```
+
+This will write `recon_2026-09.json` and print the net difference.
